WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.153
- [Instructor] In this video,

00:00:01.153 --> 00:00:02.980
we're gonna talk about one
of the most common ways

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:06.350
to measure solute
concentration in a solution.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.313
And that is molarity.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.540
And molarity is defined as
the number of moles of solute,

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.373
the thing that we are
dissolving in a solvent,

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:26.770
that divided by the liters of solution.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.800
So let's just do an example

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.130
and see if we can calculate
the molarity of a solution.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:38.640
So let's say that I have,
this is a container here.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.260
And I'm going to dissolve
some sodium sulfate in water.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.350
So sodium sulfate is the solute
and water is the solvent.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.820
Together, they give us this solution.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.780
And let's say we have a total,

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.780
the total volume of solution
is 250 milliliters of solution.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.170
And that solution is made
up of just to give ourselves

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:03.550
a bit of a refresher.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:07.790
We have the solvent, which is H2O,

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.720
it is water in this situation.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.720
And you might say, do we have
250 milliliters of water?

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.480
And the answer would be not quite

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.920
because the 250 milliliters
that's the volume of the water

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.540
plus the sodium sulfate.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:24.160
And so we're gonna have
some sodium sulfate in here.

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.280
And let's say we know

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.280
that we have 35.5 grams of sodium sulfate.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.780
That is the formula for sodium sulfate.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.530
And so given this information,

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.380
how do we figure out molarity?

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.820
Well, the first thing
you might say is okay,

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.820
I know the number of
grams of sodium sulfate.

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.680
I need to figure out the number of moles.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.240
And to figure out the number of moles,

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.730
you'd have to look at the molar mass.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:54.630
You could figure that out from
a periodic table of elements.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:56.330
But just to speed us along,

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.510
I will help you out a little bit here.

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:01.530
The molar mass sodium sulfate,

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.990
molar mass is 142.04 grams per mole.

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.960
So given everything I've now told you,

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.110
see if you can pause this video

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:20.040
and figure out the
molarity of this solution.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.203
What's the molarity of the
sodium sulfate in this solution?

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.020
All right, now let's work
through this together.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:31.020
So first, we wanna figure out
the number of moles of solute.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.250
So we can start with the mass of solute

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:35.340
that we have right over here.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:40.340
So we have 35.5 grams of sodium sulfate.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:46.360
And now if we wanna figure
out the number of moles,

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.000
see I'm gonna multiply
this times something

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.940
that would cancel out the grams.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.960
And so I don't want grams per mole.

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.090
I want moles per gram.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.160
And so I could write this.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:59.490
I could multiply this
times for every one mole

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:05.410
of sodium sulfate, NA2SO4, we have 142.04.

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:14.590
I'll write this way,
grams of sodium sulfate.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:16.920
And you can see very clearly

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.510
that that will cancel with that

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:20.870
and we're left with
moles of sodium sulfate.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.300
So we'll get a calculator out in a second

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.787
and just take 35.5 and
divide that by 142.04.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.650
And then to figure out molarity,

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.850
we wanna divide by the liters of solution.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.150
So up here we have a
calculation for number of moles

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.600
and then the liters have solution,

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:41.447
250 milliliters is the
same thing as 0.250 liters

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.590
of our solution.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.820
And now we can just use our calculator

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.170
to figure out what this is.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:55.130
35.5 divided by 142.04 equals that,

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:05.233
and then we divide that by 0.25.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.080
I could just throw a zero in there.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.750
And then that gets us
that right over there.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:12.640
And then we can think about

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.740
how many significant figures we have.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.330
So we have three over here.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.530
We have one, two, three,
four, five over here.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.960
We have three over here.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:25.170
So, I would say that we have
three significant figures.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:28.120
And so we would round this right most

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.090
or this nine right over here.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:33.973
Well, if we round that up, we get 1.00,

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.090
if we were to go to three
significant figures.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.633
So that gets us 1.00.

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:44.800
And then you might say
what is the units here?

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.600
And what people will normally
say is this is 1.00 molar.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.780
When you see this capital
M right over here,

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.960
that is the unit for more molarity

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.160
but they're really talking
about the number of moles

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.310
of solute per liter of solution.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:02.073
And we are done.

